ay everything it's  beneficial of course lots of things  aren't but never say there are many  things that were very valuable and there  are alternative accounts in the world  now which don't uh apply those those  principles in quite the same way and we  have to have a basis  um standing in the tradition and we are  we have to about understanding where we  are going with this  and there is a risk that the errors I  think we are making in terms of uh our  understanding of this relationship to  reality uh is is uh vitiating uh the  whole of our culture at some level  um and we're not I think going to Res  you know solve that until we've got an  overall story which works  right and so in the end it is about if  effectively addressing some sort of  problem but yeah you'll probably want to  shy away from the ethical vocabulary  there but it is some kind of an  improvement of some kindness yeah  certainly I think it's it's about  improving the situation we have at the  moment which is a crisis you know crisis  of understanding a crisis of what we  think you know this is these are not  trivial that they they're not just  academic they they bite and as we've  seen in the politics of the last decade  uh they're biting more and more  and they're not you know hiding from the  from the theoretical problem it's not  it's not going to overcome it so I think  we obviously  I think I'm sure there are plenty of  other people who will have uh  alternative uh Frameworks and stories to  the one that I'm putting forward but I  think we have to have some Frameworks to  help us overcome the situation we've got  and give us a sense of  um how we can uh improve and intervene  in the world uh more effectively to  achieve the things that we'd like to  achieve  yeah  okay  um well yes thank you very much
 

